Z||000000||Gold-86SE||04-22-2000||11:11 PM||||Yes, I know it is a stupid maneuver and I should have listened to that small voice in my head, but I didn't and now I have a problem.<P>This is on an '84 SE with remote deck release, but here is my problem, the remove release appears to be inoperable.<P>Before I call a locksmith, or last ditch effort drill out the lock, how can I trace down the release lock problem. I am assuming the mechanism in the trunk works.<P>Thanks for the help.||||reg||11
Z||000001||BroCar 87||04-22-2000||11:40 PM||||HEY!!!!!!!!! I believe that happened to the owner that had this fiero before me. There was a BIG A$$ hole in the decklid. I made the most of it though... filled the hole and placed hood pins in it. It was cheaper than buying a new decklid huh. I love it, It looks better too. (my opinion) Well I still have to paint it cause it still has the primer over the old hole. But it looks smoothe and slick. So....I like it.<BR>Alright      done talkin for now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>Just a suggestion for anyone that has done that or WILL do that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Zman302||04-23-2000||12:40 AM||||The power trunk release only works with the key on.  you need to find which wire is power to it and run 12v to it.  I looked in a wire diagram and it looks like it might be a orange wire that is the 12v acc wire.  you might double check this but if that is the right wire...running 12v to it and hitting the switch should release the deck.   Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||04-23-2000||02:49 AM||||My power trunk release works without having the ignition turned on.  I have an '88 GT, maybe the '84's were different?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Luperman||04-23-2000||03:06 AM||||Mine works without the key on also, 86 SE||||reg||1
Z||000005||Homicidal||04-23-2000||03:33 AM||||Mine doesn't, 84 SE.<P>I did something WORSE!  I was fiddling with the battery when hooking my amplifier up and I must have knocked one off the positive terminal and then closed the trunk.<P>I had the keys, but the trunk lock was broken for a while, so I had no POWER for the power trunk release!<P>I ended up jamming my key in far enough to make the trunk pop open.  Scary couple of minutes!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||04-23-2000||06:59 AM||||Mine works with out the key, '86 1/2 GT. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||04-23-2000||01:34 PM||||The trunk release in all 85+ cars works without the key on. This makes it rather a dangerous option to have on the car.<P>According to GM schematics. The release is interlocked with the hand brake on manual tranmisson cars. I've been told by some stick owners that this may not be true or the brake interlock is defective on most stick cars as they seem to be able to activate it regardless of pulling the brake or not.<P><BR>EMERGENCY TRUNK POWER:<P>remove relay from connector under dash. (In clip on right side of steering comlumn suport framing.)<P>hold connector so single terminal is up (like a pyramid) like this----&gt;  | _-_ |||165.121.80.178||reg||1
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||04-23-2000||03:08 PM||||Like Ogre said, those pages have now been updated.||||reg||1
Z||000009||CW85T-Type||04-24-2000||05:43 PM||||My 85 SE (v6/5spd) trunk release strangely does not work without the parking brake being activated.  <P>Chris Wilson||||reg||1
Z||000010||Patrick86GT||04-24-2000||06:19 PM||||my 86gt 4-speed remote latch is not linked to the e-brake; yet, it is linked to the ignition (when the ignition is on, the release will not function)<P>my first effort would be to unscrew the switch bezel and power it from a spare battery (connect the negative of the spare battery to the subject car as well) ||||reg||3
Z||000011||theogre||04-24-2000||06:35 PM||||CW that's exactly how it should work acording to the GM data I have.<P>Pat86, maybe I wasn't clear enough. connecting an external 12 source is what I ment above. The lower left terminal goes directly to the latch. The lower right goes to whatever interlock method is installed and provides a ground for the solinoid. The top terminal comes from the dash switch.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Gold-86SE||04-26-2000||12:27 AM||||Update to the keys in trunk fiasco.<P>I mentioned to my wife during this hunt to rescue the keys that we would end up solving her problem of the rear deck release not working - and that is exactly what we did.<P>Thanks to my 86 SE having a rear deck release switch, we recovered the keys and solved the rear deck release problem on my wife's 84 SE. <P>After dismantling the two switches, we found that on the 84 the plastic pin that extends from the rear deck release button was broken, which prevented activation of the release mechanism.<P>What a relief, I did not have to spend money for a lock smith or drill out the key hole. Now off to wal-mart to make an extra set.<P>Thanks for all the advise, fortunately it was none of the above problems.  More times than not it is like Patrick said "sometimes it's the simplest things..."||||reg||6
Z||000013||Ozzy||04-26-2000||12:55 AM||||Those rocker plastic cheesy switches are almost useless. Both my 84 SE and 87 GT have the same problem. The plastic actuator is broken off inside the switch. Does anyone know of an alternative switch that's a little more robust and in a similar style??<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
